{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>The second time</b><br>He answered and said to her: \"O you who dwell in the gardens, the companions of the shepherds have come, and they are listening to your voice. Let me hear [it].\" And she said to him: \"Flee, my beloved,\" before they notice that I am with you in the garden." "<b>The third time</b><br>\"You who dwell in gardens, companions are listening.\" Then the Shekhinah says to Kenneset Israel: \"O you who dwell in the Sanctuary, the eternal House, which is like the Throne of Glory, as in the matter of 'a glorious throne on high from the beginning' [Jeremiah 17:12] — the place of our Sanctuary.\"" "\"Companions are listening.\" The matter is that the kings long to hear your new songs, as in the matter of (Isa. 42:10) 'Sing to YHWH a new song,' and furthermore (Isa. 24:14) 'on that day this song shall be sung (to YHWH).'" "\"I too long to hear the splendor of your voice\" — and this is the matter of \"let me hear [it].\""], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:45:06.567292301Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}